*Infinite [[Shibalien Elite]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 66~66.67 seconds<sup>1,980f~2,000f</sup>.
*2 [[Shibalien Elite]]s spawn after 12 seconds<sup>360f</sup>, delay 66~66.67 seconds<sup>1,980f~2,000f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Star Peng]]s spawn after 28.67 seconds<sup>860f</sup>, delay 66~66.67 seconds<sup>1,980f~2,000f</sup>.
*2 [[Star Peng]]s spawn after 30.67 seconds<sup>920f</sup>, delay 66~66.67 seconds<sup>1,980f~2,000f</sup>.
*Infinite [[General GreGory|General GreGories]] spawn after 54 seconds<sup>1,620f</sup>, delay 66~66.67 seconds<sup>1,980f~2,000f</sup>.
*2 [[General GreGory|General GreGories]] spawn after 56 seconds<sup>1,680f</sup>, delay 66~66.67 seconds<sup>1,980f~2,000f</sup>.
*1 [[Le'Solar]] spawns after 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>.
*1 [[Corporal Weyland]] spawns after 93.33 seconds<sup>2,800f</sup>.

==Strategy==
With all [[Treasure#Details - Anti-Starred Alien Treasures|treasures for Starred Aliens]], this stage should be considerably easier than the stages required to reach it. Note, however, that this stage is still not entirely foolproof, as the Spacefish Jones spawns rather quickly with the other enemies spawning on a timer. As such, a lineup to beat this stage should have stallers ready to deploy rather quickly. Aside from basic meatshields, [[Jetpack Cat (Rare Cat)|Jetpack Cat]] works well, as he is already expected for the stage preceding this, though Jetpack can be warped. With these stallers, any strong attackers and snipers can be used to deal with the frontline threats or use them to snipe Spacefish Jones. Generally, any attackers who can take down the preceding [[Super Hyppoh]] should have no problem with these relatively weak aliens, even with their Warp and range advantage.

Also, the enemies here have barriers as strong as 40,000 HP, so a unit who can deal that much damage in a single hit or a Barrier Breaker would be necessary to beat this stage. The Breakerblast could work for this purpose, but its knockback may cause issues.

